      "video": "tablet recording",
      "summary": "The task (Grok's reading of the YOLO report):\n1. Pick up the cup and move it. 2. Pick up the blue bucket and place it onto the pen. 3. Pick up the box and move it. The actions overlap in time, so this listed order is the most likely.\n\nYOLO report:\nA person recorded a 7 s demonstration video of a task for the robot arm.\nObjects in the scene: blue bucket, cup, pen, box.\nActions, in order:\n- 1.0-6.5s: pick and move [move] cup (target)\n- 1.5-6.5s: pick and place onto [move] blue bucket (target), pen (dest)\n- 1.5-6.5s: pick and move [move] box (target)\nWhat they said: \"Uno, due, tre, L, M, O.\"\nWrite a skill that makes the robot arm reproduce this task: detect each object first, pick, place at the same destination, verify, then go home. Keep the same order. The arm's camera is on its head and it knows four objects: orange screw, blue bucket, green ring, white bucket lid; map what the person handled to the closest of these. Putting something in a cup/bucket/container means into the blue bucket; putting it to one side or on a pad means the delivery zone.",
      "tokens": 3,
      "transcript": "Uno, due, tre, L, M, O."
    }
